# The Gradle wrappers are shell scripts that now also run inside a Linux image build. This
# repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which checks text files out with
# CRLF -- and a shell script whose shebang line ends in CR fails on Linux with "bad
# interpreter", naming a path that looks correct.
#
# The committed blobs are already LF. This pins the working copy to LF as well, so a container
# built locally from that working copy behaves the same as one Render builds from a fresh
# clone. The .bat wrapper is pinned the other way for the same reason, in reverse.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
